1. Download Splunk

Download the Splunk Enterprise .deb package.

wget -O splunk.deb "<SPLUNK_DOWNLOAD_URL>"

Replace <SPLUNK_DOWNLOAD_URL> with the appropriate Splunk download URL.

2. Install Splunk

Install the downloaded Splunk package.

sudo dpkg -i splunk.deb

If dependency errors occur:

sudo apt --fix-broken install -y

Run the installation again:

sudo dpkg -i splunk.deb

3. Start Splunk

Start Splunk for the first time.

sudo /opt/splunk/bin/splunk start

Accept the Splunk license agreement and configure the Splunk administrator account.

4. Enable Splunk at Boot

Configure Splunk to start automatically when the server boots.

sudo /opt/splunk/bin/splunk enable boot-start

5. Check Splunk Status

Verify that the Splunk service is running.

sudo /opt/splunk/bin/splunk status

Expected:

splunkd is running
splunk helpers are running

6. Access Splunk Web

Open a browser and navigate to:

http://192.168.21.132:8000

7. Configure Splunk Receiving

Navigate to:

Settings
    ↓
Forwarding and receiving
    ↓
Configure receiving
    ↓
Add new receiving port

Configure the receiving port: 9997

8. Verify the Splunk Receiving Port

Check whether Splunk is listening on port 9997.

sudo ss -tulpn | grep 9997

The port should appear as listening.
